{"id":"CVE-2022-3972","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"VulDB","published":"2022-11-13T00:00:00.000Z","updated":"2025-04-14T15:56:10.156Z","title":"Pingkon HMS-PHP adminlogin.php sql injection","description":"A vulnerability was found in Pingkon HMS-PHP. It has been rated as critical. This issue affects some unknown processing of the file admin/adminlogin.php. The manipulation of the argument uname/pass leads to sql injection. The attack may be initiated remotely. The exploit has been disclosed to the public and may be used. The associated identifier of this vulnerability is VDB-213551.","cwe":["CWE-707 CWE-707 Improper Neutralization -> CWE-74 Injection -> CWE-89 SQL Injection"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.1","score":7.3,"sev":"HIGH","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"poc","Automatable":"yes","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"Pingkon","product":"HMS-PHP","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/Pingkon/HMS-PHP/issues/1"},{"url":"https://vuldb.com/?id.213551"}],"vendors":["php"]}
