{"id":"CVE-2022-29221","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"GitHub_M","published":"2022-05-24T00:00:00.000Z","updated":"2025-04-23T18:22:54.999Z","title":"PHP Code Injection by malicious block or filename in Smarty","description":"Smarty is a template engine for PHP, facilitating the separation of presentation (HTML/CSS) from application logic. Prior to versions 3.1.45 and 4.1.1, template authors could inject php code by choosing a malicious {block} name or {include} file name. Sites that cannot fully trust template authors should upgrade to versions 3.1.45 or 4.1.1 to receive a patch for this issue. There are currently no known workarounds.","cwe":["CWE-94 CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.1","score":8.8,"sev":"HIGH","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"total"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"smarty-php","product":"smarty","versions":["affected < 3.1.45","affected >= 4.0.0, < 4.1.1"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/smarty-php/smarty/security/advisories/GHSA-634x-pc3q-cf4c"},{"url":"https://github.com/smarty-php/smarty/commit/64ad6442ca1da31cefdab5c9874262b702cccddd"},{"url":"https://github.com/smarty-php/smarty/releases/tag/v3.1.45"},{"url":"https://github.com/smarty-php/smarty/releases/tag/v4.1.1"},{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2022/05/msg00044.html","tags":["mailing-list"],"name":"[debian-lts-announce] 20220529 [SECURITY] [DLA 3033-1] smarty3 security update"},{"url":"https://www.debian.org/security/2022/dsa-5151","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"DSA-5151"},{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/202209-09","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"GLSA-202209-09"},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/L777JIBIWJV34HS7LXPIDWASG7TT4LNI/","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"FEDORA-2022-52154efd61"},{"url":"https:/