{"id":"CVE-2022-31625","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"php","published":"2022-06-16T05:45:15.228Z","updated":"2024-09-16T18:35:01.122Z","title":"Freeing unallocated memory in php_pgsql_free_params()","description":"In PHP versions 7.4.x below 7.4.30, 8.0.x below 8.0.20, and 8.1.x below 8.1.7, when using Postgres database extension, supplying invalid parameters to the parametrized query may lead to PHP attempting to free memory using uninitialized data as pointers. This could lead to RCE vulnerability or denial of service.","cwe":["CWE-590 CWE-590 Free of Memory not on the Heap","CWE-824 CWE-824 Access of Uninitialized Pointer"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.1","score":8.1,"sev":"HIGH","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H"}],"affected":[{"vendor":"PHP Group","product":"PHP","versions":["affected 7.4.X <7.4.30 (custom)","affected 8.0.X <8.0.20 (custom)","affected 8.1.X <8.1.7 (custom)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://bugs.php.net/bug.php?id=81720"},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/ZZTZQKRGEYJT5UB4FGG3MOE72SQUHSL4/","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"FEDORA-2022-0a96e5b9b1"},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/3T4MMEEZYYAEHPQMZDFN44PHORJWJFZQ/","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"FEDORA-2022-f3fc52428e"},{"url":"https://www.debian.org/security/2022/dsa-5179","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"DSA-5179"},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20220722-0005/"},{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/202209-20","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"GLSA-202209-20"},{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2022/12/msg00030.html","tags":["mailing-list"],"name":"[debian-lts-announce] 20221215 [SECURITY] [DLA 3243-1] php7.3 security update"}],"configurations":["pgsql extension enabled"],"credits":["c dot fol at ambionics dot io"],"vendors":["php"]}
{"id":"CVE-2022-31626","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"php","published":"2022-06-16T05:45:16.880Z","updated":"2024-09-17T03:38:54.950Z","title":"mysqlnd/pdo password buffer overflow","description":"In PHP versions 7.4.x below 7.4.30, 8.0.x below 8.0.20, and 8.1.x below 8.1.7, when pdo_mysql extension with mysqlnd driver, if the third party is allowed to supply host to connect to and the password for the connection, password of excessive length can trigger a buffer overflow in PHP, which can lead to a remote code execution vulnerability.","cwe":["CWE-120 CWE-120 Buffer Overflow"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.1","score":7.5,"sev":"HIGH","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H"}],"affected":[{"vendor":"PHP Group","product":"PHP","versions":["affected 7.4.X <7.4.30 (custom)","affected 8.0.X <8.0.20 (custom)","affected 8.1.X <8.1.7 (custom)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://bugs.php.net/bug.php?id=81719"},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/ZZTZQKRGEYJT5UB4FGG3MOE72SQUHSL4/","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"FEDORA-2022-0a96e5b9b1"},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/3T4MMEEZYYAEHPQMZDFN44PHORJWJFZQ/","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"FEDORA-2022-f3fc52428e"},{"url":"https://www.debian.org/security/2022/dsa-5179","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"DSA-5179"},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20220722-0005/"},{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/202209-20","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"GLSA-202209-20"},{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2022/12/msg00030.html","tags":["mailing-list"],"name":"[debian-lts-announce] 20221215 [SECURITY] [DLA 3243-1] php7.3 security update"}],"configurations":["pgsql extension enabled"],"credits":["c dot fol at ambionics dot io"],"vendors":["php"]}
{"id":"CVE-2022-31627","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"php","published":"2022-07-28T05:50:09.522Z","updated":"2024-09-16T21:02:46.605Z","title":"Heap buffer overflow in finfo_buffer","description":"In PHP versions 8.1.x below 8.1.8, when fileinfo functions, such as finfo_buffer, due to incorrect patch applied to the third party code from libmagic, incorrect function may be used to free allocated memory, which may lead to heap corruption.","cwe":["CWE-590 CWE-590 Free of Memory not on the Heap"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.1","score":7.7,"sev":"HIGH","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:L"}],"affected":[{"vendor":"PHP Group","product":"PHP","versions":["affected 8.1.X <8.1.8 (custom)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://bugs.php.net/bug.php?id=81723","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20220826-0008/","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/202209-20","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_GENTOO"],"name":"GLSA-202209-20"}],"credits":["reported by xd4rker at gmail dot com"],"vendors":["php"]}
